{"encoding":"verislop.autonomous-critique/0.1","verdict":"REPAIR","counterexamples":[],"corrections":[{"diagnostic_index":0,"artifact":"proposal.lean","explanation":"The theorem `VeriSlopAST.solve_spec` is currently a `sorry` (unproven). The implementation `solve` is definitionally equal to the right-hand side of the specification (it constructs the Output using the exact same `List.filter`, `List.map`, `List.sum`, and `List.length` expressions). Therefore, the proof can be completed by replacing `by sorry` with `by intros; constructor <;> rfl` (or simply `by intros; rfl` if the conjunction unfolds definitionally). This provides the executable guarantee required for the postconditions O1-O7 and I1."}]}